name: Partial inventory retains history and excludes unsafe paths, with explicit recovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_containment.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 30 context:build indexed 1 file | context-produced
submit: run pack:suggest-shards {}
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 30 never auto-installed | draft-produced
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_containment.py @TMP_TARGET @ART capture
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_containment.py @TMP_TARGET @ART redirect
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 30 context:build partial inventory | context-partial
submit: run pack:suggest-shards {}
require-live-snap: 30 PARTIAL inventory | draft-partial
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_containment.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial
paste-file: @ART/failed-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Outcome · partial | retained-failure
resize: 160x48
live-snap: failure-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: failure-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: failure-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: failure-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: failure-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: failure-page-two-40x12
ask: Does the partial reader show the excluded path and retain its original evidence without implying complete coverage?
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_containment.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restore
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 30 context:build indexed 1 file | rebuilt
submit: context status
require-live-snap: 30 Enumeration: Git tracked files | restored-context
expect: Sample: 1 of 1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_containment.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial-recovered
keys: C-c
require-exit: 15
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
paste-file: @ART/failed-replay.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Outcome · partial | historical-failure
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/inventory_containment.py @TMP_TARGET @ART partial-restarted
ask: Does restart preserve the original partial receipt separately from the later explicit context rebuild?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 15
